## 4. Microstrip W x c at h over a plane, eps = 1, per mm: the trial against a P1 (5-point) energy
  The discrete energy of any admissible grid function is >= C of the boxed problem >= C in the open;
  so trial >= P1 energy shows trial >= truth. The inscribed wire (radius c/2) is a lower reference.
    h=0.075: trial 8.3264 >= P1-in-box 5.8639 >= truth; inscribed wire 3.4676; trial/P1 1.420; holds: True
    h=0.1: trial 7.2343 >= P1-in-box 4.9670 >= truth; inscribed wire 3.1015; trial/P1 1.456; holds: True
    h=0.15: trial 6.2404 >= P1-in-box 4.0115 >= truth; inscribed wire 2.6747; trial/P1 1.556; holds: True
    h=0.2: trial 5.8416 >= P1-in-box 3.4976 >= truth; inscribed wire 2.4243; trial/P1 1.670; holds: True

